* SPDX-License-Identifier: CERN-OHL-P-2.0
* Behavioural models for the drone power board simulations. NOT vendor models.
* Every parameter is fitted to one datasheet number (noted) or is an
* assumption (noted). The README lists what these can and cannot show.

* IPT012N08N5 x 2 in parallel (Infineon DS v2.1): VTO = VGS(th) typ 3.0 V
* (range 2.2-3.8 V is handled in scripts/pdb_calc.py); KP so the pair gives
* RDS(on) = 0.6 mOhm (two x 1.2 mOhm max) at VGS = 10 V:
*   KP = 1 / (0.0006 * (10 - 3.0)) = 238 A/V^2
.model IPT012X2 NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=3.0 KP=238 LAMBDA=0.001)
* Gate capacitance stand-in: 2 x Ciss typ 13 nF (VDS = 40 V). Miller charge
* is not modelled; it is small here because VDS is already low at turn-on.

* BUK7M42-60E (Nexperia): VTO = VGS(th) typ 3.0 V; RDS(on) 42 mOhm max at 10 V
*   KP = 1 / (0.042 * 7) = 3.4 A/V^2
.model BUK7M42 NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=3.0 KP=3.4 LAMBDA=0.001)

* Body-diode stand-ins (assumption, generic)
.model DBODYM D(IS=1e-8 N=1.2 RS=1m)
.model DBODYP D(IS=1e-10 N=1.2 RS=50m)

* BZX84-C12: VZ 11.4-12.7 V at 5 mA; model 12.0 V (assumption, mid-range)
.model BZX84C12 D(IS=1e-14 N=1 RS=20 BV=12.0 IBV=5m)

* 1N4148W (Vishay 85748): VF 1.0 V max at 10 mA. Generic small-signal fit.
.model D1N4148W D(IS=2.5n N=1.75 RS=0.6 BV=100)

* SS36 (Vishay 88751): one datasheet point only, VF = 0.75 V max at 3 A.
* N and RS are ASSUMED; IS fitted so the model gives 0.75 V at 3 A:
*   0.6 V across the junction + 3 A x 0.05 ohm
.model SS36 D(IS=1.5u N=1.6 RS=0.05 CJO=200p BV=60)

* TPS54360 high-side switch: RDS(on) 190 mOhm max (VIN 12 V, BOOT-SW 6 V)
.model SWHS SW(RON=0.190 ROFF=1e6 VT=0.5 VH=0.1)
